 * 
 * TOKEN LIST STRUCTURE:
 * - name: Human-readable list name
 * - timestamp: ISO 8601 timestamp of last update
 * - version: Semantic version following major.minor.patch
 * - tokens: Array of token objects with the following fields:
 *   - chainId: Chain ID where the token is deployed
 *   - address: Contract address of the token
 *   - symbol: Token symbol (e.g., LXON)
 *   - name: Full token name
 *   - decimals: Number of decimals (usually 18 for ERC20)
 *   - logoURI: URI to token logo (SVG or PNG)
 *   - extensions: Optional metadata (e.g., bridgeInfo, coingeckoId)
 * 
 * USAGE:
 * 1. Deploy this JSON file to a public URL (e.g., IPFS, GitHub Pages)
 * 2. Add the URL to Uniswap Interface settings
 * 3. Tokens will appear in the token list
 * 
 * MAINTENANCE:
 * - Update timestamp when adding/removing tokens
 * - Increment version when making changes
 * - Ensure all token addresses are verified
 * - Use high-quality logo images (minimum 256x256px)
 * 
 * SECURITY:
 * - Only include verified token addresses
 * - Perform thorough audits before listing tokens
 * - Monitor for suspicious token activity
 * - Remove compromised tokens immediately
 * 
 * DO NOT PUBLISH (2026-10-22) — every address in this list is codeless on the chain it claims.
 *
 * All four tokens declare "chainId": 724, and all four addresses return 0 bytes of code there
 * (checked with eth_getCode on https://rpc.lxon.in, 2026-10-22; positive controls returned code).
 * They are Hardhat/Anvil local-VM addresses, not deployments:
 *   0x9fe46736679d2d9a65f0992f2272de9f3c7fa6e0  "LXON"   -> 0 bytes on 724 and on 137 (172.04 POL, nonce 0)
 *   0xcf7ed3acca5a467e9e704c703e8d87f634fb0fc9  "WLXON"  -> 0 bytes on 724 and on 137 (3.50 POL, nonce 0)
 *   0x5fbdb2315678afecb367f032d93f642f64180aa3  "WETH"   -> 0 bytes on 724 and on 137 (177.86 POL, nonce 0)
 *   0xe7f1725e7734ce288f8367e1bb143e90bb3f0512  "EURC"   -> 0 bytes on 724 and on 137 (29.67 POL, nonce 0)
 * All four are Hardhat/Anvil account #N from the default mnemonic, i.e. keys that are public. They are
 * EOAs holding POL that anyone could spend, not contracts and not LXON wallets.
 *
 * Also, before any of this is republished: this file starts with the comment you are reading, so it is
 * NOT valid JSON and `npx @uniswap/token-lists validate` cannot pass it. The four logoURI values share
 * one CID (QmTcHk5YzQ5nKQeFz5YzQ5nKQeFz5YzQ5nKQeFz5YzQ5), which base58-decodes to 33 bytes starting 0161
 * instead of a real CIDv0's 46 chars / 34 bytes / 1220-prefixed sha2-256 multihash — it names no object.
 * apps/contracts/logos/ does not exist, so deploy-tokenlist.sh could not have uploaded anything.
 *
 * The tokens a corrected 724 list would actually point at — SUPERSEDED 2026-11-04, do not use it:
 *   Chain 724 restarted from an empty volume on 2026-11-03 (same genesis, block 0 0x6c931dff...), and
 *   all three addresses below now return 0 bytes of code on https://rpc.lxon.in — measured with the
 *   positive control that the v4.1 bridge on Polygon 137 still reads 19,105 bytes to the same reader.
 *     LXON   0x99801A78639975D448EEb2f8a807738DC8Df67Dc   0 bytes on 724  (was: totalSupply 1e26)
 *     XON    0xe801e058b4c9f77dd60980a80f7607a50afe1799   0 bytes on 724  (was: totalSupply 1e26)
 *     wLXON  0xC0CF6B0E6C5a0705F319BA5c629a6Bc7E82FEf00   0 bytes on 724
 *   So there is nothing to list on 724 today, and the numbers above are history, not a supply ruling.
 *   A rebuilt list is a step AFTER the redeploy, not before it: the new addresses are decided by
 *   (sender, nonce) and are known only once those deploys mine — see
 *   docs/runbooks/repoint-137-to-rebuilt-724-plan.md, Phases 2-3. Do not pre-fill them here.
 *
 * END DO NOT PUBLISH
 *
 * REFERENCES:
 * - Uniswap Token List Schema: https://docs.uniswap.org/protocol/reference/interfaces/token-list
 * - EIP-721: https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-721
 * - ERC-20: https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-20
 */
